Rachael the Healer started out pretty good but an early wand of
wishing on DL-3 was obviously the major help to getting to this
ascension.  A scroll of charging, blessed +2 SDSM, Blessed +2 Cloak of
Protection, Blessed +2 Speed Boots, MagicBane.  The wand had one more
charge but I held off at that point to continue on with the protection
racket.

I made it to Mine town with no difficulties and contributed to the
cross-aligned altar for 7 points of protection.  Then it was back up
to the main trunk to find Sokoban.  I completed Sokoban again easily
with the use of 2 pets and got my BOH in the top level zoo.

After Sokoban I traveled down the main trunk locating the quest level
(and Magic Portal) and going down so far as Medusa's just to know the
distance and map out levels.  No Big Room was generated in this game.
There were very little "You hear someone counting money" messages I
figured that there was no portal to Fort Ludios either.

I worked at leveling Rachael up to 12 and then dug under the Medusas
Swamp as I still had not found any means of Levitation.  Though I had
reflection I still employed my towel before stepping back upstairs to
meet with Medusa.  Perseus' statue did not have any boots so I used a
wish to get the Ring of Levitation.  Then it was down to find the
Castle.  Pet killed the eels for me then it was time to enter.

I used the backdoor floating over the trap doors.  Cleared the dragons
in the side rooms, gaining shock resistance and cold resistance, then
opened the door and took on the zoo.  The fight was mostly without
excitement, some previous nurse-dancing had gotten hit points up to a
safe enough level so I just stood at the door in the choke point and
swung away with Magicbane.  A wand of Death took care of the Lich and
Demilich.  I used the castle WoW to get an "oLS.

The first mistake of the game happened here.  I forgot to put my =oLev
back on and tried to go back out the back door only to fall into The
Valley.  I landed just next to the stairs but a Shiny Spellbook caught
Rachael's eyes so even though there were vampires approaching, I
picked it up and read it.  Ugh, she was frozen in place and the
vampires burned out her "oLS along with over 200 HP until she could
move again!  I quickly dispatched the Vamps and hauled back upstairs.
Used a wish to get another "oLS

A long climb got Rachael back to the first level of Sokoban where a
reverse genocide of Nurse's resulted in a big no-teleporting, square-
dance and a lot more HP's.

Now it was time for the Quest and all I can say is that it was
uneventful as well.  Pets helped with cleaning up some of the corspe
messes and the Quest Leader fell quickly to a /oDeath.

Just to say I did it, I went back to the mines and finished up down to
the Mines End, getting a luck stone.

Figuring there were no other distractions in the main dungeon I
started back down the main branch and found a couple of vaults along
the way, one of which teleported into Fort Ludios.  The first monster
through the door was a 'trice who was nice enough to leave a corpse so
dispatching the remainder of critters and Soldiers was so easy.
Blocked up the entrance to the Zoo with a ?oEarth and Croesus fell
with ease to MagicBane.  Only one quarter of the vault was cleared,
just too much weight from gold to haul anymore.

Back in the Main branch a black pudding was spotted on a co-aligned
altar level.  Having never farmed before I gave it a shot.  The altar
room was perfect shaped for the farm so we went at it for a few
thousand turns with a simple dull knife.  It got boring quickly so I
cant say I got any remarkable drops but with all of the sacrificing I
was granted: Mjollner, Vorpal Blade, StormBringer(i think) and one two
more artifacts that were mostly left in my big stash pile behind the
altar.  This was the point where she Crowned as well.

I figured now was as good as time as any to start the run.

Jublix swamp was 2 levels below the Valley, Asmodeus was 2 levels
below him, Balzaabub was three below that.  Orcus town was just one or
two levels beyond.  I thought Rachael killed Jub with a /oDigging
through his tummy but he re-appeared in Orcus town where he most
certainly was destroyed.  There were bribes for the other demons and
Orcus took a shot from a  /oDeath.

Towers were in sight quickly and I had no problems clearing out Vlad's
tower and Vlad with the help of a pet Minotaur.  Found the lowest
level at DL49 and only a short search located the Vibrating Square.

At this point Rachael was burdened and there was no choice but to
unload the incredible amount of gold she was hauling around.  She used
the Eye to beam back to the main branch, dumped the gold at DL9 by the
stairs then walked back down to Gehenomen for one last look for usable
items.  Picked up another "oLS

Rodney's tower was wiped out with a Rubber Chick corpse but Rodney
required a shot from the /oDeath after it rotted away.  Got the Book
and then it was back to the Square.  Performed the ritual and another
'trice corpse helped clear the very bottom.  Grabbed the One True
Amulet, zapped Rodney again with Death, found another "oLS and then
the race was on.

There was a lot of being pulled back down levels but I had cleared
nice paths between the staircases in Gehenomen so it wasn't too bad.
Rodney turned up once here and once more in the Main Dungeon (/oDeath
x2).  There was one pit stop at DL9 to make some more Holy Water that
mostly went untouched.  Finally, she stepped out of the Dungeon and
faced the plain or Earth.  I have been on this plane 3 other times.

All I can say is the Plains were easy this time.  On the final run
Rachael was level 22, had 359 HP's lots of Death wands which were
saved for the Astral Plain.

Drawing on past experiences there was little fighting on my part.  The
Plane of Air was probably the hardest because of the air Elementals
but when one beat her up to bad there was always a shocking sphere or
steam vortex to camp in to recover HP.  The portal was found the old
fashioned way.  I have been on this Plain 2 other times.

Plane of Fire:  again, not too bad.  Just moved to stay away from the
mob until a Salamander disappeared from site and then ran for that
portal.  I have been on this Plain one other time.

Plane of Water:  New Ground, never seen it before.  It wasnt too hard
to move around and stay away from the eels and such, killing water
elementals as I could.  Mostly I just followed the bubble until i
triggered the Portal and in all it was over with in 100-200 turns.

This was it, I had never made it this far.  I knew there would be
Angels beyond and of course the Riders but as for details, they were
few in my mind.  Rachael stepped into the Portal...

I was very surprised to find a tame Angel to greet her.  Like I said,
I have never been here before, but reading other posts I knew there
were three altars, only one co-aligned.  Quaffed the last two potions
of Gain Level and bravely she fought her way to the left and found a
door.  Warning told her there were some Baddies on the other side but
when it opened I was not expecting to find Death!  I knew my wand of
Death would be useless and I wasnt sure how to deal with Him, so I ran
away and luckily he did not follow.

Back-tracking I found a door in the center and opened that.  A fight
with a Priest, then Pestilence touched Rachael once.  The Staff took
care of the Sickness, and the /oDeath took care of Pestilence.  An Elf-
Lord firing a /oDeath helped to clear some of the mob and Rachel moved
forward and entered the Temple door.  Within, A giant through a
boulder and blocked off  the door so no Mob followed me in, it was
just Rachael and the Priest (after the giant was dispatched).  I could
not believe it, here was the Neutral Altar!  I regret not using my
Magic Whistle to call my Angel in before offering but I was too
excited.

